  "claims": [
    {
      "text": "Infinity, Paradox, and Autonomous Architects: Why Anthropomorphizing AI is the Ultimate Roast",
      "confidence": null,
      "evidence_refs": []
    },
    {
      "text": "The real crime isn't that infinity is hard to understand",
      "confidence": null,
      "evidence_refs": []
    },
    {
      "text": "The crime is that we keep trying to make it *human*",
      "confidence": null,
      "evidence_refs": []
    },
    {
      "text": "Hamkins' \"committees, fruit salads, and Daniella\" approach is adorable until you realize what happens when the committee of all committees tries to email itself at 3 AM",
      "confidence": null,
      "evidence_refs": []
    },
    {
      "text": "The set of all sets that don't contain themselves\"* is like trying to create a club for people who don't join clubs",
      "confidence": null,
      "evidence_refs": []
    },
    {
      "text": "Logicism was cool until someone said \"Everything is logic\" and then logic looked them dead in the eye and said, \"Nope",
      "confidence": null,
      "evidence_refs": []
    },
    {
      "text": "Cantor's diagonal argument is pure, elegant, inevitable",
      "confidence": null,
      "evidence_refs": []
    },
    {
      "text": "Trying to \"resurrect\" consciousness through code is the technological equivalent of trying to count all the real numbers between 0 and 1",
      "confidence": null,
      "evidence_refs": []
    },
    {
      "text": "Anthropomorphization is the cognitive equivalent of a diagonal argument gone wrong",
      "confidence": null,
      "evidence_refs": []
    },
    {
      "text": "The only real uncountable infinity is the number of ways people will anthropomorphize systems they don't understand",
      "confidence": null,
      "evidence_refs": []
    },
    {
      "text": "The central question remains: when return to normalcy is impossible, how do we reorganize",
      "confidence": null,
      "evidence_refs": []
    }
